@doc smysl/0.1 {
  id: v/f12
  intent: code-review
  lang: en
  requires: ["smysl.kernel/0.1", "x.code/v1"]
  roots: [d/pin]
}

# A corpus typed by an extension schema rather than by the kernel. Until 1.7 these units were
# not in any retrieval index at all — absent rather than filtered — so `find` returned nothing
# for them and said nothing about why. A kernel claim sits beside them so the two readings of
# `--kind` and `--schema` can be told apart.

@schema x.code/v1 { version: 1, types: ["x.code/decision", "x.code/consequence"] }

@claim c/kernel { status: speculative }
~ The connection pool saturated under load.

@x.code/decision d/pin { status: speculative }
~ Pin the connection pool size rather than tracking the range.

@x.code/consequence k/churn { status: speculative }
~ Connection pool churn becomes a deliberate act.
